# Path guard.
#
# This file does one job: it names, as globs, the places where non-public
# layers are allowed to exist on a working machine, so that they cannot be
# staged by accident. It is not a substitute for the content guard in
# hooks/pre-commit — a path guard only knows where a file is, not what is in
# it, and material arrives in the wrong directory routinely.

# --- the real literal deny-list: never publishable, by construction ---
config/literals.json
config/*.local.json

# --- non-public layers (boundary rule: measured values are public, raw logs
#     are private, and calibration values are private even though they are
#     measured values) ---
/calibration/
/operational/
/raw-logs/
/live-ledger/
/corpus/
/private/
/transcripts/
*.local.*

# --- generated by running the gates, not content ---
# `make check` writes this. Committing it would publish a snapshot that is
# stale the moment anything changes, and a stale audit is worse than none.
records/tautological_control_audit.json

# --- working artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
